<h1>Build outbound notification calls with VoiceML.</h1>
<p class="lede">A fictional high school&rsquo;s Dean of Students calls home about an absence. One API request places the call; answering-machine detection decides whether to leave a voicemail or talk to a person; and a person can confirm the message or be put through to the attendance office. The call flow is two documents published on voiceml.org, with no application server.</p>
<p class="hero-actions">
	<a class="btn btn-primary" href="/signup/">Free trial</a>
	<a class="btn btn-secondary" href="{{ site.voicemlReferenceUrl }}/nouns/number/">Machine detection reference</a>
</p>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>What the call does</h2>
	<ul class="features-grid">
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "code-slash" %}</span>
			<h3>One request per call</h3>
			<p>A single REST API request places the call and names the document to run when it is answered.</p>
		</li>
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "robot" %}</span>
			<h3>Person or voicemail</h3>
			<p>Answering-machine detection reports who answered as <code>AnsweredBy</code>, before the document runs.</p>
		</li>
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "record-circle" %}</span>
			<h3>A message after the beep</h3>
			<p>On voicemail, the document waits for the greeting to end, then leaves the full message.</p>
		</li>
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "hash" %}</span>
			<h3>A reply on the keypad</h3>
			<p>A person can press 1 to confirm, or 2 to be connected to the attendance office.</p>
		</li>
	</ul>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>How the pieces fit</h2>
	<div class="table-container">
		<table class="data-table">
			<caption>Components of the attendance calls</caption>
			<thead>
				<tr>
					<th scope="col">Piece</th>
					<th scope="col">Where it lives</th>
					<th scope="col">What it does</th>
				</tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td>API request</td><td>Your terminal, a script, or a scheduled job</td><td>Places each call, with machine detection on.</td></tr>
				<tr><td>Notice document</td><td>voiceml.org, <code>/r/</code> URL</td><td>Runs when the call is answered. Leaves a voicemail, or asks a person to reply.</td></tr>
				<tr><td>Response document</td><td>voiceml.org, <code>/r/</code> URL</td><td>The <code>action</code> of the reply <code>&lt;Gather&gt;</code>. Thanks the person or connects them to the office.</td></tr>
				<tr><td>Attendance office</td><td>Any phone number</td><td>Rings when a person presses 2.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Before you start</h2>
	<ol>
		<li><strong>A VoiceML account with a phone number</strong>, to place the calls from. See <a href="/voiceml/">VoiceML</a> or <a href="/signup/">start a free trial</a>.</li>
		<li><strong>The Account SID and API key</strong>, for the API request.</li>
		<li><strong>Consent from the people you call.</strong> Automated and prerecorded calls need the recipient&rsquo;s prior express consent. See <a href="/support/voice/compliance/">compliance and abuse prevention</a> before you place calls to anyone but yourself.</li>
	</ol>
	<div class="alert alert-warning" role="note">
		<p><strong>The numbers in these documents and the request are fictional.</strong> They use the 555-0100 to 555-0199 range, which is set aside for fiction. Test by calling your own phone first.</p>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Step 1: Publish the response document</h2>
	<p>Replace the attendance office&rsquo;s number with your own, then publish it at <a href="{{ site.voicemlPublisherUrl }}">voiceml.org</a>. It contains Liquid tags, so it is published to an <code>/r/</code> URL. Keep the URL exactly as returned, <code>key</code> included, and don&rsquo;t post it publicly.</p>
	<p class="code-block-header">response.xml</p>
	<pre class="code-block" data-lang="xml"><code>{{ voicemlSamples["attendance-calls"].response | escape }}</code></pre>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Step 2: Publish the notice document</h2>
	<p>Replace <code>RESPONSE_URL</code> with the <code>/r/</code> URL from step 1, then publish.</p>
	<p class="code-block-header">notice.xml</p>
	<pre class="code-block" data-lang="xml"><code>{{ voicemlSamples["attendance-calls"].notice | escape }}</code></pre>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Step 3: Place a call</h2>
	<p>Send this request with your Account SID, API key, phone numbers, and the notice document&rsquo;s <code>/r/</code> URL in place of <code>NOTICE_URL</code>. <code>From</code> must be a number on your account or a caller ID verified on it; any other number is refused with error 21210. Start with your own mobile as <code>To</code>.</p>
	<p class="code-block-header">Place the call</p>
	<pre class="code-block" data-lang="bash"><code>ACCOUNT_SID="AC..."
API_KEY="..."

curl -u "$ACCOUNT_SID:$API_KEY" \
  -d "To=+13125550199" \
  -d "From=+13125550100" \
  -d "Url=NOTICE_URL" \
  -d "MachineDetection=DetectMessageEnd" \
  {{ site.voicemlPortalUrl }}/2010-04-01/Accounts/$ACCOUNT_SID/Calls</code></pre>
	<p>Answer it to hear the menu and press 1 or 2. Place it again and let it go to voicemail to hear the message left after your greeting.</p>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>How detection picks the message</h2>
	<p>With <code>MachineDetection</code> in the request, the call waits for a verdict before running the document, and the verdict arrives with the request for <code>NOTICE_URL</code> as <code>AnsweredBy</code>. The notice document branches on it:</p>
	<div class="table-container">
		<table class="data-table">
			<caption>What each AnsweredBy value does</caption>
			<thead>
				<tr>
					<th scope="col"><code>AnsweredBy</code></th>
					<th scope="col">What happens</th>
				</tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>human</code></td><td>The menu: press 1 to confirm, or 2 for the attendance office.</td></tr>
				<tr><td>Starts with <code>machine</code></td><td>The voicemail message, then the call ends.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>fax</code></td><td>The call ends.</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>unknown</code></td><td>The menu, so a person who wasn&rsquo;t recognized still hears it.</td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
	</div>
	<p><code>MachineDetection=DetectMessageEnd</code> waits for the voicemail greeting to finish before reporting a machine, so the message starts after the beep instead of over the greeting. <code>MachineDetection=Enable</code> reports sooner and suits calls that hang up on machines. The detection thresholds and timeout are the same settings as the <code>&lt;Number&gt;</code> noun&rsquo;s machine detection.</p>
</section>

