<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Limits of this design</h2>
	<ul>
		<li><strong>Every call says the same thing.</strong> A voiceml.org document can&rsquo;t receive values of your own, such as a student&rsquo;s name, so a personal message needs one document per message, or a server.</li>
		<li><strong>Replies aren&rsquo;t recorded.</strong> Pressing 1 is acknowledged on the call, but nothing stores it. To keep a list of who confirmed, point the <code>&lt;Gather&gt;</code>&rsquo;s <code>action</code> at your own server.</li>
		<li><strong>One request places one call.</strong> Calling a list means sending one request per number, from a script or scheduler.</li>
		<li><strong>Detection can be wrong.</strong> A person who answers with a long greeting can be taken for voicemail, and a short voicemail greeting for a person. The voicemail message is written to make sense either way.</li>
	</ul>
</section>

